**Read:** [Simultaneous rheology and cure kinetics — Romberg and Kotula, 2023](../sources/Rheology-and-Cure-Kinetics-Romberg-Kotula.lingua#r_17JNF4M1B6SKKEWAMQAXB3B614) and [Epoxy conversion from rheology — Romberg and colleagues, 2024](../sources/Epoxy-Conversion-Models-Romberg-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_2P4B2NBQT7APB3CQ2KDQ6MGMX0), including methods and model comparisons. Revisit spectroscopy, thermal analysis and rheometry.

A residual calorimetric exotherm, a reactive Raman band and a storage modulus measure different aspects of material state. Instrument response, baseline, reference signal, temperature and sample preparation enter their interpretation. A relation fitted between conversion and modulus can change with filler, frequency or network architecture.

**Work:** Reconstruct a full conversion calculation from a documented spectrum or thermal measurement, distinguishing raw observations from digitized published curves. Repeat the inference with a justified alternate baseline or normalization. Compare the resulting conversion uncertainty with the uncertainty in a deformation or final-state prediction. Reserve a thermal history or filler condition for prediction. State clearly if raw data cannot be retrieved; do not silently replace missing measurements with fabricated ones.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
